# What the coherence review of Rebel keeps (M-rebel-library's item 31): every
# finding of the instruments of `suite_rebel.hero` that the review did not
# repair, each with its reason, for the readers who come after it, one reader
# per layer who has not written it. A finding the tree shows and this list does
# not hold is a failure of the `rebel` suite, and so is an entry here the tree
# no longer shows. Written by the review of 2026-11-19 from the readout of
# `rebel_review.hero` over Rebel 0.1.0; every reason is one of the constants
# below, each saying why the repair is not local and sure, or where it is
# repaired. The review's fix lanes of 2026-11-20 (its plan's § 8) took out
# every row their repairs retired, keep the findings they made new with
# their reasons, and corrected five reasons its readers found wrong though
# the keep held (L-E02). The rules lane of the D wave (step 86g, 2026-11-21)
# took out the 58 rows the D wave retired, 30 of them the abbreviations
# README § A3 lets stand since D06, and kept the 22 findings its lanes made,
# the spans' helpers and the test servers' fixtures among them.

# A finding the review keeps: the instrument's check, the key it is kept
# under (what the readout prints after `under`), and the reason.
record Kept
    check: str
    key: str
    why: str

# A face past the size: a split is no local repair.
constant A_SPLIT_IS_NOT_LOCAL: str
    "a split moves names every program that uses the package writes, so it is no local repair; kept for the readers, who weigh it against the reference libraries' own sizes"

# One name in `unicode` and `strings`, for a character and for a text.
constant CHARACTER_AND_TEXT: str
    "`unicode` asks of one character and `strings` of a text: one meaning at two sizes, which the parameter's name says (`c`, `s`), as README § A3's one name, one meaning asks"

# One name for one question asked of different grammars.
constant EACH_ITS_GRAMMAR: str
    "each answers for its own grammar or format (JSON, jq, JSONPath, SemVer, YAML; MQTT's and NATS's subjects; HTTP's and PDF's dates; GraphQL's and JSON-RPC's requests over HTTP; the standard's quoted identifier and MySQL's): one meaning, by design"

# Each client reads its own service's environment.
constant EACH_ITS_SERVICE: str
    "each client reads its own service's variables from the environment, by design"

# A deadline set by the package that made the stream.
constant EACH_ITS_STREAM: str
    "each sets the deadline of the streams its own package makes, over the one `io.Stream`: `ipc`'s channel, and `tls`'s TLS stream or a connection's (since 2026-11-20, the coherence review's X12), which `io` leaves to the package that made the stream (`io.hero`'s doc); `net.set_deadline` takes milliseconds at layer 3 since D07 and is no twin of these; the readers ask whether `io` should own the word"

# Formats read into and written from `json.Value`.
constant FORMATS_OF_ONE_VALUE: str
    "each format read into or written from the one `json.Value`, by design (`yaml`'s row of README § A1)"

# A ledger naming another package's function and a helper of its own.
constant NAMES_HTTPS: str
    "`web.ledger` names `http.respond_redirect` and adds `web.path_for`, a route's path: one capability, `http`'s, counted for `web` by the helper beside it"

# One body in packages with no public home below them for it.
constant NO_PUBLIC_HOME: str
    "one helper in packages that may not share a private module (README § A2), and no package below them offers it publicly: made one only by giving it a public home, which is the readers' choice"

# The one API every member of a family keeps.
constant ONE_API_BY_DESIGN: str
    "the one shape every member of a family keeps, so a program moves from one to another by its `use` line: each compression format, each image format, each tokenizer table a subpackage of its own so a program carries the one it uses (README § A2)"

# `math/linear`'s types, combined by its functions.
constant ONE_DOMAIN_OF_TYPES: str
    "`math/linear`'s types are combined by its functions (`mul_mat4_vec4`), one domain a split would make use itself across packages; without overloading the type's name stands in each function's name"

# Two packages of one layer, which may not use each other.
constant ONE_LAYER: str
    "two packages of one layer may not use each other (README § A1), so what they share is written twice until a package below both holds it publicly: the readers'"

# An abbreviated parameter, whose name callers write.
constant PARAMETER_LABELS: str
    "a parameter's name is a label a caller writes where two parameters share a type (spec § 9), so the rename reaches callers in other packages and the examples: no local repair; kept for the readers, who choose the word"

# A percentage written plainly and as a language writes it.
constant PLAIN_AND_LOCALE: str
    "`numbers.format_percent` writes one fixed form and `i18n/numbers.format_percent` the form a language writes: whether the plain one is the root locale's is the readers' question, and either repair moves a name callers write"

# The tables of `tokenizer/tables`, each a module a program names alone.
constant TABLES_OF_A_PACKAGE: str
    "a table of `tokenizer/tables`, data a program names alone so that it carries the one it uses; as a package of its own it would stand below `tokenizer/tables` and use that package's private modules (`made`, its data), which README § A1's layers refuse, so its row and ledger are the readers' question: one package with four faces, or the private modules moved under each table"

# `web`'s middleware, which takes the request first.
constant REQUEST_FIRST: str
    "`web`'s middleware takes the request first and the response it changes second, as every handler of the package; a reorder moves every call, and is the readers' question"

# Retries an LLM client waits as its server asks.
constant RETRIES_OF_THEIR_OWN: str
    "`http.Retries` is the general policy, and the two LLM clients wait what their server asks; whether they should hold an `http.Retries` is the readers' question"

# A test fixture of a package's own tests.
constant TEST_FIXTURES: str
    "a fixture of each package's own tests (a canned server, a loopback listener) that no program reaches; one home for test fixtures is the readers' question"

# `big`'s three exact numbers.
constant THREE_EXACT_NUMBERS: str
    "`big` holds three exact numbers, `Integer`, `Decimal` and `Fraction`, whose conversions name two at once (`decimal_of_fraction`): a split into subpackages is the readers' question, and moves names callers write"

# The two LLM clients, built to answer the same questions.
constant TWO_LLM_CLIENTS: str
    "`llm/anthropic` and `llm/openai` are two clients of two APIs built to answer the same questions, each through its own types, by design (README § A1's two rows)"

# One word, two meanings.
constant TWO_MEANINGS: str
    "one word, two meanings: what each says it does differs (the finding quotes both), so neither answers the other's question; the readers decide whether one of the names should change"

# Vectors for geometry and vectors for embeddings.
constant TWO_SHAPES_OF_VECTOR: str
    "`math/linear` holds vectors of two to four `f64` for geometry and `vectors` lists of `f32` of any length for embeddings: one operation on two shapes, which a language without overloading writes twice; the readers decide whether the ledgers should name each other"

# A total step over bytes already valid, in a hot loop.
constant A_TOTAL_STEP: str
    "a public form exists (`unicode.utf8_len_of_first`, `unicode.utf8_len`) and answers an `i64?` that fails on what begins no character, where these copies are total steps over text already valid inside a loop over every byte: kept for the step's cost, which is unmeasured and the readers' to time"

# A table looked up by a direct comparison.
constant A_DIRECT_COMPARISON: str
    "`lists.upper_bound` is the public home, through a function value at every comparison; each copy looks up a table of its own by a direct comparison, a speed kept until it is timed (fix-plan § 10, unrun)"

# A span made into a door's milliseconds or a protocol's seconds.
constant SPANS_TO_DOORS: str
    "a `time.Duration` made into the whole milliseconds a door of `net` or `tls` takes, or the whole seconds a protocol writes, a part of one rounding up so that no wait is shorter than asked, and no bound made into the door's own: the helper D07's spans needed (steps 88a to 88j) in packages that may not share a private module, and `time` offers none publicly (`to_units` truncates and names no door's bound); a public one in `time` is the readers' choice"

# A maker the author's answer A made of a copy.
constant MAKER_SINCE_THE_SPLIT: str
    "since the author's answer A of 2026-11-21 split `net.Address` into `Host` and `Address` (step 88i), `with_port` makes an `Address` of a `Host` and a port, a maker and no copy; README § A3 names a maker by its type's noun, `address`, a rename of `net`'s face, which another lane held when this row was written (step 86g): the next lane's"

# Every finding kept, in the order the readout prints them.
function kept() -> [Kept]
    return [
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "bits/count in containers/bits, math", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "client/base-url in llm/anthropic, llm/openai", why: TWO_LLM_CLIENTS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "client/env in llm/anthropic, llm/openai, s3", why: EACH_ITS_SERVICE)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "client/headers in llm/anthropic, llm/openai", why: TWO_LLM_CLIENTS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "client/key in llm/anthropic, llm/openai", why: TWO_LLM_CLIENTS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "client/retries in http, llm/anthropic, llm/openai", why: RETRIES_OF_THEIR_OWN)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "client/timeout in llm/anthropic, llm/openai", why: TWO_LLM_CLIENTS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "client/transport in llm/anthropic, llm/openai", why: TWO_LLM_CLIENTS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "date/parse in http, i18n/dates", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "document/operations in graphql, openapi", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "errors/advice in llm/anthropic, llm/openai", why: TWO_LLM_CLIENTS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "errors/codes in http2, jsonrpc", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "errors/connection in llm/anthropic, llm/openai", why: TWO_LLM_CLIENTS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "errors/status in llm/anthropic, llm/openai", why: TWO_LLM_CLIENTS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "http/client in graphql, jsonrpc", why: EACH_ITS_GRAMMAR)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "http/server in graphql, jsonrpc", why: EACH_ITS_GRAMMAR)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "message/values in jsonrpc, protobuf", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "name/reverse in dns, net", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "number/percent in i18n/numbers, numbers", why: PLAIN_AND_LOCALE)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "options in grpc, http2", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "random/bytes in os, random", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "raw/request in llm/anthropic, llm/openai", why: TWO_LLM_CLIENTS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "response/json in graphql, http", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "response/redirect in http, web", why: NAMES_HTTPS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "server/dispatch in grpc, jsonrpc, mcp", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "status/text in http, process", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "structured-output in llm/anthropic, llm/openai", why: TWO_LLM_CLIENTS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "text/words in strings, unicode/segment", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "vector/arithmetic in math/linear, vectors", why: TWO_SHAPES_OF_VECTOR)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "vector/dot in math/linear, vectors", why: TWO_SHAPES_OF_VECTOR)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "vector/normalize in math/linear, vectors", why: TWO_SHAPES_OF_VECTOR)
        Kept(check: "ledgers", key: "write/json in openapi, websocket", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "compare in path, strings", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "decode in image/bmp, image/netpbm", why: ONE_API_BY_DESIGN)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "decode_image in image/bmp, image/gif, image/jpeg, image/netpbm, image/png", why: ONE_API_BY_DESIGN)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "decompress in compress/brotli, compress/bzip2, compress/lz4, compress/xz, compress/zstd", why: ONE_API_BY_DESIGN)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "encoding in tokenizer/tables/cl100k_base, tokenizer/tables/o200k_base, tokenizer/tables/o200k_harmony", why: ONE_API_BY_DESIGN)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "error_name in http2, kafka", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "escape in html, regex", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "format in json, yaml", why: FORMATS_OF_ONE_VALUE)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "format_date in http, pdf", why: EACH_ITS_GRAMMAR)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "frame_size in compress/lz4, compress/zstd", why: ONE_API_BY_DESIGN)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "is_ascii in strings, unicode", why: CHARACTER_AND_TEXT)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "is_lower in strings, unicode", why: CHARACTER_AND_TEXT)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "is_upper in strings, unicode", why: CHARACTER_AND_TEXT)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "is_valid in json, json/jq, json/path, semver, yaml", why: EACH_ITS_GRAMMAR)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "is_valid_filter in mqtt, nats", why: EACH_ITS_GRAMMAR)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "labels_of in dns, unicode/encodings", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "matches in mqtt, nats", why: EACH_ITS_GRAMMAR)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "name in path, unicode/names", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "names in tokenizer/tables, unicode/encodings", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "parse in json, yaml", why: FORMATS_OF_ONE_VALUE)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "parse_date in http, pdf", why: EACH_ITS_GRAMMAR)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "quote in json, process", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "quote_identifier in sql, sql/mysql", why: EACH_ITS_GRAMMAR)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "remove_all in fs, keyring", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "set_deadline in ipc, tls", why: EACH_ITS_STREAM)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "skippable_frame in compress/lz4, compress/zstd", why: ONE_API_BY_DESIGN)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "to_casefold in strings, unicode", why: CHARACTER_AND_TEXT)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "to_lower in strings, unicode", why: CHARACTER_AND_TEXT)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "to_title in strings, unicode", why: CHARACTER_AND_TEXT)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "to_upper in strings, unicode", why: CHARACTER_AND_TEXT)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "unescape in url, xml", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "twins", key: "words in strings, unicode/segment", why: TWO_MEANINGS)
        Kept(check: "prefixed", key: "big Decimal", why: THREE_EXACT_NUMBERS)
        Kept(check: "prefixed", key: "big Fraction", why: THREE_EXACT_NUMBERS)
        Kept(check: "prefixed", key: "math/linear Vec2", why: ONE_DOMAIN_OF_TYPES)
        Kept(check: "prefixed", key: "math/linear Vec3", why: ONE_DOMAIN_OF_TYPES)
        Kept(check: "prefixed", key: "math/linear Vec4", why: ONE_DOMAIN_OF_TYPES)
        Kept(check: "prefixed", key: "math/linear Mat3", why: ONE_DOMAIN_OF_TYPES)
        Kept(check: "prefixed", key: "math/linear Mat4", why: ONE_DOMAIN_OF_TYPES)
        Kept(check: "oversized", key: "bytes", why: A_SPLIT_IS_NOT_LOCAL)
        Kept(check: "oversized", key: "http", why: A_SPLIT_IS_NOT_LOCAL)
        Kept(check: "oversized", key: "math", why: A_SPLIT_IS_NOT_LOCAL)
        Kept(check: "oversized", key: "math/linear", why: A_SPLIT_IS_NOT_LOCAL)
        Kept(check: "oversized", key: "mcp", why: A_SPLIT_IS_NOT_LOCAL)
        Kept(check: "oversized", key: "net", why: A_SPLIT_IS_NOT_LOCAL)
        Kept(check: "oversized", key: "openapi", why: A_SPLIT_IS_NOT_LOCAL)
        Kept(check: "oversized", key: "pdf", why: A_SPLIT_IS_NOT_LOCAL)
        Kept(check: "oversized", key: "protobuf", why: A_SPLIT_IS_NOT_LOCAL)
        Kept(check: "oversized", key: "strings", why: A_SPLIT_IS_NOT_LOCAL)
        Kept(check: "names", key: "grpc abbreviated conn", why: PARAMETER_LABELS)
        Kept(check: "names", key: "net copy with_port", why: MAKER_SINCE_THE_SPLIT)
        Kept(check: "names", key: "web copy with_cors", why: REQUEST_FIRST)
        Kept(check: "names", key: "web copy with_etag", why: REQUEST_FIRST)
        Kept(check: "unlisted", key: "no row tokenizer/tables/cl100k_base", why: TABLES_OF_A_PACKAGE)
        Kept(check: "unlisted", key: "no ledger tokenizer/tables/cl100k_base", why: TABLES_OF_A_PACKAGE)
        Kept(check: "unlisted", key: "no row tokenizer/tables/o200k_base", why: TABLES_OF_A_PACKAGE)
        Kept(check: "unlisted", key: "no ledger tokenizer/tables/o200k_base", why: TABLES_OF_A_PACKAGE)
        Kept(check: "unlisted", key: "no row tokenizer/tables/o200k_harmony", why: TABLES_OF_A_PACKAGE)
        Kept(check: "unlisted", key: "no ledger tokenizer/tables/o200k_harmony", why: TABLES_OF_A_PACKAGE)
        Kept(check: "bodies", key: "amqp/internal/link.ms_of, mqtt/internal/link.ms_of, nats/internal/link.ms_of, redis/internal/session.whole_ms", why: SPANS_TO_DOORS)
